      "math_academy_id": "e-15642",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/22e71949f4a63a7f650c38841bd67d3e5cb415a5c8819b0ea4ce80431bf6dbfb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\overline{AD}$ is a segment, what is the measure of $\\angle FOD?$",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14190698/assets/416aef1d024c1b926eb33bada7611bb1d345b0d9daa2d59730b05bab85617c05.png)\n\nTwo angles are supplementary if their measures add up to $180^\\circ,$ a straight angle.\n\nSince $\\overline{AD}$ is a segment, we have that $\\angle AOF$ and $\\angle FOD$ are supplementary. \n\n$$\nm \\angle AOF + m \\angle FOD = 180^\\circ\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of $\\angle FOD$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠FOD & ={180}^{∘}-m∠AOF \\\\  & ={180}^{∘}-{45}^{∘} \\\\  & ={135}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
